"""Locked-build program sources for the behavior-local particle texture
inputs and per-behavior base-color memories the published CDN pin (1.0.286)
predates.

Upstream Noisemaker c4f7cdd7 gives the points agent behaviors their own
diffuse/field texture inputs: each program samples `diffuseTex` through a
`selectedDiffuse` helper gated on `diffuseActive`, and reads the field map
from `fieldTex`/`heightTex` gated on `fieldActive` instead of plain
`inputTex`. Upstream 12751c78 adds a per-behavior base-color memory: each
agent reads `baseColorTex`, writes `outBaseColor` through a `keptBaseColor`
helper gated on `diffuseActive`, and falls back to the remembered color when
the fresh color write would lose it. dla, flow, and physarum rename their
field-map parameter and sampler to the upstream `heightTex` name. The locked
build's program text lacks that behavior, so the transpiler substitutes the
newer program source verbatim. Each entry fires only when the incoming source
is the locked build's exact program text (see
build._LOCKED_BUILD_PROGRAM_SOURCES) and falls through to the shared
matrix-temp and vector-read tail passes.
"""

